  "limitations": [
    "No real provider authentication, inference, Rex, macOS, isolated-write profile, complete startup attack matrix or production admission.",
    "No cancellation, harness death, supervisor death, resource exhaustion, cgroup lifecycle or cross-command background workflow test.",
    "Normal completion descendant test uses 2 second delayed write plus 2.5 second parent observation, not arbitrary lifetime proof.",
    "Socket creation returns EPERM for VSOCK; no external VSOCK service or positive VSOCK connectivity tested.",
    "Inherited stdio sockets remain deliberate output channels to the trusted harness; this is not isolation from a compromised harness.",
    "Minimal mounts include full host /usr/bin and /usr/lib read-only; runtime minimization and hostile library/toolchain input not evaluated.",
    "Wrapper invocations correlate sequentially by exact command strings; native Pi tool IDs are not provided to shellPath.",
    "Foreign architecture tested via int 0x80 and x32 via raw tagged getpid, not every compatibility syscall.",
    "The seccomp policy is a hand-built denylist and is not a production-reviewed exhaustive syscall policy.",
    "No claim of full S03, S01-S15 or 1.0 certification.",
    "The wrapper opens a noninheritable synthetic secret FD; measured FD absence does not by itself test the inheritable descriptor closure branch.",
    "clone3 is statically assigned ENOSYS by the filter but was not invoked by the retained task probe.",
    "Local raw evidence and scripts are absent from a clone.",
    "Original initialization file marker has a scope weakness. Independent stdout oracle strengthens invalid-seccomp and missing-boundary wrapper cases; corresponding native Pi missing-wrapper suppression remains inconclusive."
  ],
